Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Section 3.5 Derive", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085065559998`*^9, {3.402852451862959*^9, 
   3.4028524527508025`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b03225a9-7a43-4cf2-9fea-\
eb02a196b128"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Deriving Formulas in Mathematica",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506599*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e8f59b6a-05ee-45f6-82b5-dfc55198e4a5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Deriving Formulas in Mathematica", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066140003`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0811090b-987a-4822-a302-\
6111496f1e04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398408506627*^9, 3.39840851899*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1361]:=",ExpressionUUID->"caf1d39b-fdd1-46d7-8a16-735991ad11a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One of the most powerful features in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the ability to derive extremely complicated formulas simply and easily \
using basic theory.   However, it seems that this incredibly useful feature \
must be delayed until a ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " user has gained sufficient familiarity with the ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " syntax so as not to get lost.  Several preliminary observations are \
required before this process becomes easy.  Specifically, a ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " user must make the transition from \"hand derivations\" to ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "derivations.\n\nUsually, \"hand derivations\" involve writing equations, \
substitutions and algebraic simplifications.  \n\nOn paper, a formula is ",
 StyleBox["entered",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " as:\n\tlhs = rhs\nHowever, in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " equations are entered as:\n\tlhs == rhs\nbecause \"=\" means assignment, \
not equality which is entered as \"==\".   Remember, equality is a \
\"logical\" operation, and not an \"assignment\" operation.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Substitution",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " is achieved either by:\n\t ",
 StyleBox["Assignment:",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "\n\t \tlhs == rhs\n\t \t...\n\t \ta = value\n\t \tf[x_] := something\n\t \t\
...\n\t \tnewEquation   =    lhs[...,a,...,f[x],...] == \
rhs[...,a,...,f[x],...]\n\t \t...\n\t (Now newEquation contains:   \
lhs[...,value,...,something,...] == rhs[...,value,...,something,...])\n\n\t ",
 StyleBox["Replacement rules:",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "\n\t \t...\n\t \tnewEquation   =    lhs[...,a,...] == rhs[...,a,...]   /.  \
a \[Rule] value\n\t \tnewEquation   =    lhs[...,f[x],...] == \
rhs[...,f[x],...]   /.  f[x] \[Rule] something     (note the \"x\" and not \
\"x_\")\n\t \t...\n\t (Now newEquation contains:   \
lhs[...,value,...,something,...] == rhs[...,value,...,something,...])\n\t \
(Remember, you must re-assign the result so that it can be used later.)\n\t \n\
Algebraic ",
 StyleBox["simplification",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " can be achieved by:\n\tlhs == rhs  // Simplify\n\tlhs == rhs  // \
FullSimplify\n\t\nHowever, you need to realize the following points about the \
use of \"==\" related to simplification.\n",
 StyleBox["First",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", the head of \"==\" is \"Equal\" and that it is a logical operator:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066400003`*^9, {3.402851380350772*^9, 
   3.4028513805695705`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32db746d-d5a5-4818-822e-\
89aa2918441b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", "\[Equal]", "b"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066400003`*^9, {3.4028514058721123`*^9, 3.4028514179842*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1362]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b9556012-7000-4e6c-85f8-d6f94e7c5208"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Second",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", that the properties of  \"==\" do not ",
 StyleBox["automatically",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " allow cancellation and simplification between the lhs and rhs.\nFor \
example, consider the following two cases:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066400003`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ee78c9bb-960a-460b-8603-\
9639c849c076"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "lhs"}], "==", 
  RowBox[{"3", "+", "rhs"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066400003`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1363]:=",ExpressionUUID->"05c9334d-3bb1-4d36-a0bc-ea0d4132e16c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "lhs"}], "==", 
   RowBox[{"3", "+", "rhs"}]}], "   ", "//", " ", "Simplify"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066400003`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1364]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f222eb2a-6160-46fc-baa6-2ab2591d8f2e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore, it is usually ",
 StyleBox["desirable",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " to move all of the equation to just one side, so that simplification and \
cancellation can be performed:\n\tlhs  -  rhs  ==  0"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066400003`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3abeed24-fe5c-4d69-a63c-\
fa613e6c4aea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "lhs"}], ")"}], "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"3", "+", "rhs"}], ")"}]}], "  ", "==", "  ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506641*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1365]:=",ExpressionUUID->"186c1eb0-f46e-4a8d-9cfe-f915d12a5ed2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remark:  Moving all of the equation to just one side will ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " be necessary if your subsequent ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands directly manipulate the full equation (i.e. for example:   Solve, \
DSolve, NDSolve etc.).\n\n",
 StyleBox["Third",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", you will often want to operate on both sides of the equation (i.e. \
multiply, divide, differentiate, integrate etc.).  However, the Equal command \
does not ",
 StyleBox["automatically",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " thread over other ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands.  \nThis is illustrated by the following examples: "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506641*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3e9059c8-8ac2-4a71-8b10-3c34b97c656c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"3", "*", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"lhs", " ", "==", " ", "rhs"}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506641*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1366]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7e33dfd6-608a-4325-bb03-c8cbc2be3f46"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"lhs1", " ", "==", " ", "rhs1"}], ")"}], "  ", "+", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"lhs2", " ", "==", " ", "rhs2"}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506641*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1367]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f1333d90-7700-4bab-bacb-28ccb140b6a9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"lhs1", " ", "==", " ", "rhs1"}], ")"}], "  ", "*", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"lhs2", " ", "==", " ", "rhs2"}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506641*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1368]:=",ExpressionUUID->"53fd7835-151b-4652-9186-5fc9c11962ca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "==", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "  ", "+", "  ", "1"}]}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506641*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1369]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b22aaab0-4ac7-4db9-bacf-9539a5e713c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore, you must ",
 StyleBox["explicitly",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " tell ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to do this.  \nBefore showing you how to do this, consider the FullForm of \
the starting ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " expression:  "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506642*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d319c6c6-2f48-4493-8d50-45fbd43cef36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"3", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs", " ", "==", " ", "rhs"}], ")"}]}], "   ", "//", 
   "FullForm"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506642*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1370]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fa3ebd45-c182-4db5-b7d7-2075f6142f51"],

Cell["\<\
Note that the \"Times\" command is on the outside and the \"Equal\" command \
is on the inside.  
Next, consider the FullForm of the expression that you want:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506642*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f0fdd980-c62a-4695-9c63-676a8872c266"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"3", "*", "lhs"}], "==", 
   RowBox[{"3", "*", "rhs"}]}], "   ", "//", "FullForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506642*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1371]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f4a5cef5-72c0-4cd5-9c32-afb2e6138d63"],

Cell["\<\
Note that the \"Equal\" command is on the outside and the \"Times\" command \
is on the inside.  
It is clear that you want to distribute (i.e. thread) the \"Times[3, ... ]\" \
over the  \"Equal[lhs,rhs]\".
This can be accomplished by using the Thread command:
\t Thread[  lhs == rhs,  Equal ]       (Remember, \"Equal\" is the head of \
\"==\")\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506642*^9},ExpressionUUID->"07404432-f539-47f4-9f67-a8c2ffb46678"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Thread", "[", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"3", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs", " ", "==", " ", "rhs"}], ")"}]}], ",", "  ", "Equal"}], 
  " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506642*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1372]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6deedd9f-c075-4f29-b708-834c3009bbc6"],

Cell["Consider the other examples:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398408506642*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3824b959-f24b-4af6-9eac-414099349877"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Thread", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs1", " ", "==", " ", "rhs1"}], ")"}], "  ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs2", " ", "==", " ", "rhs2"}], ")"}]}], ",", "  ", "Equal"}], 
  " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398408506642*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1373]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fe317889-bf42-4dd0-bdf2-233b98ac704d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Thread", "[", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs1", " ", "==", " ", "rhs1"}], ")"}], "  ", "*", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"lhs2", " ", "==", " ", "rhs2"}], ")"}]}], ",", "  ", "Equal"}], 
  " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066429996`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1374]:=",ExpressionUUID->"854dafbf-5918-455f-a025-d523ef0b1474"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Thread", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}], ",", "  ", "Equal"}], " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066429996`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1375]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e2953955-7271-4266-9ad7-a040b0e8f428"],

Cell["\<\
Using the above observations will usually let you derive even the most \
demanding formulas.

Finally, if your work demands repeated use of threading over the Equal \
command, then it may be convenient to define your own function which will \
accomplish this task automatically:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066429996`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"102b8f90-2f63-4d57-8b28-\
29cccc321336"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"threadEqual", "[", "equation_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Thread", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"equation", ",", "  ", "Equal"}], " ", "]"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066429996`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1376]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ad911dda-d7ca-4af0-818f-afd8596de683"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "==", 
      RowBox[{"1", "+", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}]}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}], " ", "//", 
  "threadEqual"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3984085066429996`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1377]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6017079d-9361-4606-8f29-6d27bb25fdc6"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Example: Derivation of the Single Pendulum Formula", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3984085066429996`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"82ce5c1f-0099-4f41-a6c2-\
b30811417c9d"],

Cell["\<\
Consider the simple mechanical problem of one pendulum attached to the \
ceiling.  We would like to derive the equations of motion for this problem.  \
See Figure 1.3 on page 7 of the book for the diagram.  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.749557902224064*^9},ExpressionUUID->"fcf85e4c-4efb-44de-92a7-\
59ed7bd645fc"],

